Description: seahub: fixed FHS paths for the data, cache and media trees
 Upstream assumes one mutable install tree: MEDIA_ROOT is the shipped media/
 directory with avatars/ and custom/ symlinked into seahub-data, itself
 located relative to the install tree, and thumbnails are written next to
 them.
 Here the shipped media and the collected assets stay read-only in the
 install tree (MEDIA_ROOT), avatars and custom branding live in
 SEAHUB_DATA_ROOT (taken from the SEAHUB_DATA_DIR environment variable, so
 the data directory can be relocated), and the regenerable thumbnails live
 in /var/cache/seafile. Each /media/ subtree is served from the setting that
 owns it; the custom-branding lookups and the default file storage use
 SEAHUB_DATA_ROOT directly, so no symlink into the install tree is needed.
Author: dionysius <dragon.dionysius@gmail.com>
Forwarded: not-needed
Comment: install-layout specific, not something upstream's own tar.gz/docker install needs.
